tour.steps_label: Tutorial steps
tour.step1.label: How UniSearch helps
tour.step1.kicker: Welcome
tour.step1.title: Start with a clear plan
tour.step1.desc: UniSearch helps you choose bachelor's universities that fit your goals. You do not need to know where to begin: work through the same simple route every time.
tour.step1.point1: Tell us what matters to you in your profile.
tour.step1.point2: Browse widely, then use filters to narrow the list.
tour.step1.point3: Open promising universities, compare them, and check the details before you apply.
tour.step2.label: Build your profile
tour.step2.kicker: First, tell us about you
tour.step2.title: Fill in your profile
tour.step2.desc: Your profile gives the catalog useful context. Add only the information you already know; you can return and improve it later.
tour.step2.point1: Start with the subject you want to study, your budget, and GPA if you have it.
tour.step2.point2: Add language and entrance-exam results when available.
tour.step2.point3: More complete data makes {fit} and {chance} more useful; missing data is never treated as a zero.
tour.step3.label: Explore choices
tour.step3.kicker: Then, browse broadly
tour.step3.title: Search for an idea, not a perfect answer
tour.step3.desc: Use the search field when you already have a university or city in mind. Otherwise, start with the list: it is normal to explore first and decide later.
tour.step3.point1: Each result is a university you can open for fuller information.
tour.step3.point2: Use List to scan names and facts; switch to Map when location is important.
tour.step3.point3: When your profile is ready, sort by {fit} to see the most relevant options first.
tour.step4.label: Narrow the list
tour.step4.kicker: Make the list manageable
tour.step4.title: Use filters one decision at a time
tour.step4.desc: Filters update the results so you can focus on realistic choices. Begin with the few constraints that matter most, then add more only when you need them.
tour.step4.point1: Choose countries or cities you would genuinely consider.
tour.step4.point2: Set a tuition range and funding preference to keep costs realistic.
tour.step4.point3: Use subject and other filters after the basics; clear or adjust any filter whenever the list becomes too small.
tour.step5.label: Check the details
tour.step5.kicker: Before you shortlist
tour.step5.title: Open a university and read the evidence
tour.step5.desc: A card shows the essentials. Open the university to view admission requirements, tuition fees, and available funding options.
tour.step5.point1: Review admission requirements and choose the relevant admission option.
tour.step5.point2: Use {chance} as an estimate, not a guarantee of admission.
tour.step5.point3: Compare tuition, scholarships, and other costs with the information shown for that university.
tour.step6.label: Choose confidently
tour.step6.kicker: Your final short list
tour.step6.title: Compare a few realistic options
tour.step6.desc: Keep several universities in view rather than chasing one perfect choice. Comparison makes the trade-offs between fit, admission requirements, and costs easier to see.
tour.step6.point1: Use Compare to place promising universities side by side.
tour.step6.point2: Keep a balanced list: ambitious, realistic, and safer choices.
tour.step6.point3: Return to your profile or filters whenever your priorities change.
